## ⚠️ One important decision for the next two stages

I would **not** turn CoinDesk into an over-engineered distributed system yet.

We'll build a **modular production architecture first**, prove it locally, then introduce orchestration/containers/infrastructure only where the workload actually requires it.

That's important because **Stage 13 is the big transition**: we're going from one source (CoinDesk) to a **multi-source financial data collection platform**. The roadmap explicitly places Federal Reserve, ECB, BOE, BOJ, BLS, FRED, Treasury, ForexFactory, SEC, Yahoo Finance, Binance, CoinGecko, and many others after the production-scraper foundation. 

So **Stage 12 + Stage 13 together are the architecture-defining part of the course**. We should prioritize correctness, clean boundaries, and extensibility over adding fancy infrastructure too early. 🚀
